deliver groceries to customers.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:15.400
-Ooh.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:16.934
-It's pretty cool, actually.

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.634
The driverless trucks
will pick up items from Walmart

00:02:19.634 --> 00:02:23.267
and then deliver them right
through your living-room wall.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.534
What?!

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:26.834
-Oh, yeah!

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:27.834
-Oh, yeah!

00:02:27.834 --> 00:02:30.000
-Oh, yeah!
-Yeah.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.801
Walmart is the only place you'll
find cutting-edge technology

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.934
and also a barefoot guy
buying margarita mix.

00:02:36.834 --> 00:02:38.267
"I'm surprised
it's not more packed here

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.267
at 3:00 in the morning."

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.667
Hey, I saw that,
guys, restaurants

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.267
are facing a shortage because of

00:02:44.267 --> 00:02:46.534
supply-chain issues
of takeout containers.

00:02:46.534 --> 00:02:47.901
-Ooh!

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.968
-Yeah, that will be fun when
the Uber Eats guy is like,

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.767
"Here's your fries.

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:55.133
Put it on your lap
or you want it..."

00:02:57.067 --> 00:02:58.667
